52, MOF- $177^{48}$ , MOF- $205^{48}$ , MOF- $210^{48}$ , MOF-5195, and NU-11149. The BBB framework provides the highest total methane gravimetric uptakes $53\mathrm{\mt{\%}}$ , $45\mathrm{\mt{\%}}$ , $26~\mathrm{wt\%}$ ) of the designed frameworks, see Figure 5(a,c,e), however, lower total methane volumetric uptakes. The blue lines highlight a trend of decreasing total methane gravimetric and increasing total methane volumetric uptakes. The best balanced (gravimetric-volumetric) total methane uptakes are observed for the TT, TB, and BB frameworks, which are also balanced with respect to the working capacity, see Figure 5(b,d,f).
